  "articleBody": "Kitchen remodeling often requires opening walls to run new circuits, shift plumbing lines, or replace worn materials. However, drywall installation is not just cosmetic; it creates the structural base for your cabinets and backsplashes. Knowing when to bring in an experienced contractor keeps your remodel on track.\n\nSignals You Need Professional Drywall Work\n- Hidden Water Damage: Dark staining or softened gypsum behind your dishwasher or sink indicates long-term moisture issues that require sub-surface inspection before hanging new board.\n- Rerouted Utilities: Moving your range, adding dedicated small-appliance circuits, or relocating sink supply lines means walls should only be sealed after trades finish rough-ins.\n- Heavy Cabinet Support: Hanging upper cabinets requires verified stud layouts and structural backing blocks securely fastened inside the wall cavities.\n- Uneven Wall Surfaces: Older framing frequently bows, creating wavy walls that make tile backsplashes and countertop scribing uneven.\n- Large Fire-Separation Walls: Kitchens adjoining garages or utility chases often demand specific fire-rated drywall thicknesses and fastener spacing.\n\nWhat to Do Next\nIf your kitchen walls need structural backing, utility coordination, or extensive taping to prepare for cabinetry, bringing in an experienced team prevents costly rework. Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC provides hands-on remodeling and finish drywall services across the Denver area. Call 303-505-0866 to review your kitchen project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
